In article <6813@kielouta.fi>, f1toyl@uta.fi (Topi Ylinen) writes:
|> As a long-time Moria addict, I recently downloaded Hack from one FTP site.
|> The problem is, I do not get any graphics on my PC 286 (which has a VGA
|> driver, btw). The program works normally, I can do anything, but the screen
|> just does not display any "picture". It does display various messages, though.
|> The Moria I downloaded from the same site works normally (the graphics too) 
|> meanwhile Larn seems to suffer this same malady...
|> 
|> I guess it has to do with the setup. Can anyone tell me what to do with
|> the configuration file?
|> 
|> Thanks in advance....
|> 

Sounds like your missing the line:

DEVICE=C:\DOS\ANSI.SYS

from your config.sys file.  Add it and everything should work.  Moria doesn't
need this because it doesn't use Ansi to output to the screen.

(Note:  If you get a chance, pick up Nansi from an archive site.  It is a much
faster version of ansi, and Larn supports some extras.  Last time I checked,
it was zipped up with Larn.)


